      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Orchestrator-workers",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Orchestrator-workers",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "created": 1791802801645,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "T38xO2_0jbQev8C84AFzl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -9086.797620851557,
      "y": 5951.7426580263855,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "DHvboM8O9zixNBzU7J6ST",
        "AX3SbdxsVTfS87GEnnpv4",
        "Ii5B34YqydHJ_Gzavft6k",
        "Wyh-tyPiCX6IcnjtL5uUk",
        "cY_4wYEpEvvT7F9z3tCbB",
        "Dyku1fvLTGmkH5gCmlCg5",
        "1gX4jYWDcuM31Qjem8uHk",
        "OjfAP0GR4A25gXd76_Xtm"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2124245759,
      "version": 8971,
      "versionNonce": 1420923217,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792409321299,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In the orchestrator-workers workflow, a central LLM dynamically breaks down tasks, delegates them to\nworker LLMs, and synthesizes their results.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis workflow is well-suited for complex tasks where you can’t predict the subtasks needed (in coding,\nfor example, the number of files that need to be changed and the nature of the change in each file likely\ndepend on the task). Whereas it’s topographically similar, the key difference from parallelization is its\nflexibility—subtasks aren't pre-defined, but determined by the orchestrator based on the specific input.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In the orchestrator-workers workflow, a central LLM dynamically breaks down tasks, delegates them to worker LLMs, and synthesizes their results.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis workflow is well-suited for complex tasks where you can’t predict the subtasks needed (in coding, for example, the number of files that need to be changed and the nature of the change in each file likely depend on the task). Whereas it’s topographically similar, the key difference from parallelization is its flexibility—subtasks aren't pre-defined, but determined by the orchestrator based on the specific input.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1791802801645,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
