      "text": "Multi Agent Systems",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Multi Agent Systems",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vx87OTuNpkcvZiX6qL50J",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1166.8120815452312,
      "y": 8539.496044985364,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "QBXYAiytWvc6pNehvs65o",
        "eGxTvWK817XD8cBoxlrfk",
        "43WkKDoMaY24X2h9xHy1O",
        "udRjTBZkra304TYOtxfZm",
        "MaiW8-8EXyJuSoLF686Df",
        "135yuXSBRwd9haxav8Ccl",
        "eXuIQgcIYdevFoi4Us4lX",
        "niNsnsAtgnBk9VqLCeNba",
        "DGxclwwUIPjPJ_frOTA00"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1896749023,
      "version": 9296,
      "versionNonce": 1254867103,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792409321299,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Multi-agent architectures coordinate multiple specialized agents to tackle complex problems that exceed\nthe capabilities of a single generalist system.\n\nRather than one AI model handling everything, tasks are decomposed, distributed, and executed across\nmultiple agents, often with distinct expertise for specific types of queries. The results from multiple\nagents are then synthesized into a coherent response.\n\nMulti-agent systems organize around two fundamental coordination concepts: centralized and\ndecentralized architectures.\n\nCentralized systems employ hierarchical patterns where a central supervisor intelligently delegates tasks\nto specialized agents, creating clear chains of responsibility that mirror effective human organizational\nstructures. . These hierarchical systems are known by various names such as supervisory, orchestrator,\nor router patterns.\n\nDecentralized systems use collaborative patterns where autonomous agents communicate directly in peer-\nto-peer fashion, negotiate roles dynamically, and solve complex problems through distributed intelligence.\nCollaborative systems are sometimes termed swarm or federated architectures",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Multi-agent architectures coordinate multiple specialized agents to tackle complex problems that exceed the capabilities of a single generalist system.\n\nRather than one AI model handling everything, tasks are decomposed, distributed, and executed across multiple agents, often with distinct expertise for specific types of queries. The results from multiple agents are then synthesized into a coherent response.\n\nMulti-agent systems organize around two fundamental coordination concepts: centralized and decentralized architectures.\n\nCentralized systems employ hierarchical patterns where a central supervisor intelligently delegates tasks to specialized agents, creating clear chains of responsibility that mirror effective human organizational structures. . These hierarchical systems are known by various names such as supervisory, orchestrator, or router patterns.\n\nDecentralized systems use collaborative patterns where autonomous agents communicate directly in peer-to-peer fashion, negotiate roles dynamically, and solve complex problems through distributed intelligence. Collaborative systems are sometimes termed swarm or federated architectures",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1791803438988,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
