    {
      "id": "D9-KQZNVLf1fEWIH6F-RU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3481.2700635117108,
      "y": 7623.335755269971,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 1725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "XE8j7cPQbhPzJQHsgfFQq",
        "GZj8u1rSq_BTlEto9Whf-",
        "cPFnwp2slyoyPupiP3h7c",
        "ye6_T-YzEbgrJpyq-QpxB",
        "iiJocl-w10Eflx26XdK_Q",
        "YudwWqYwQgj_rBBqXlobt",
        "laczaHZRGuoEQrCJLKunQ",
        "0c958Csg8NEwl4EyNQ1MF",
        "ntxkQjkx06jnH60LAQ_or",
        "S7eqK83CzAiQ4XkJpEXW7",
        "Xjtwu4le83J621-7_EwJT"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b91",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 348850175,
      "version": 9271,
      "versionNonce": 420027089,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792409321299,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A decoder-only Transformer operates in two phases: Prefil and decoding.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPrefill: All prompt tokens are processed through the Transformer. At each position t, the final layer\nproduces a contextual representation:\n\n\n\n\n\nThe model then projects the final hidden representation into vocabulary logits:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe proposed readout takes a final hidden vector h and produces logits:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ninstead of predicting one of potentially hundreds of thousands of vocabulary tokens, it predicts one of\nK allowed decisions.\n\nWhy not simply use the probabilities of the tokens corresponding to the answers?\nFor example, if the alternatives are:\n    - YES\n    - NO\nWe could take the vocabulary logits for the tokens representing YES and NO, normalize them, and obtain\ntwo probabilities. However, Jev supports arbitrary natural-language answer options, including lengthy\ndescriptions. A decision may involve comparing concepts represented by many tokens rather than\nchoosing between two fixed vocabulary tokens.\n\nSuppose we have one input document and 50 independent questions about it. The causal Transformer is\nparticularly convenient here because all questions can reuse the same prefix KV cache.\nEach branch can access the state and its own question, without accessing sibling questions.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A decoder-only Transformer operates in two phases: Prefil and decoding.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPrefill: All prompt tokens are processed through the Transformer. At each position t, the final layer produces a contextual representation:\n\n\n\n\n\nThe model then projects the final hidden representation into vocabulary logits:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe proposed readout takes a final hidden vector h and produces logits:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ninstead of predicting one of potentially hundreds of thousands of vocabulary tokens, it predicts one of K allowed decisions.\n\nWhy not simply use the probabilities of the tokens corresponding to the answers?\nFor example, if the alternatives are:\n    - YES\n    - NO\nWe could take the vocabulary logits for the tokens representing YES and NO, normalize them, and obtain two probabilities. However, Jev supports arbitrary natural-language answer options, including lengthy descriptions. A decision may involve comparing concepts represented by many tokens rather than choosing between two fixed vocabulary tokens.\n\nSuppose we have one input document and 50 independent questions about it. The causal Transformer is particularly convenient here because all questions can reuse the same prefix KV cache.\nEach branch can access the state and its own question, without accessing sibling questions.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1791877268891,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
