      "seed": 1403889055,
      "version": 163,
      "versionNonce": 1107689855,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792409321299,
      "created": 1791878523650,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "JevBench",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "JevBench",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rJ4xaRyQcs0Hu1L7uTtDi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3466.0780723508033,
      "y": 6323.954255955803,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 1075,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "ozjbnc_SIwadoi73Qj0m_",
        "5Q4cE6R-fRyNhmD4h5Put",
        "06E4Pkwv1G94JfCC87AKp",
        "lnoeS2eC7KwoYLJJ_96nF",
        "4ZSWcePpt1vtdndewQ0Zv",
        "_YySrKQpdXDMKBzcbD06O",
        "K-llgfuVtSo2RLru5HIRH",
        "emVxvUs6wj2NRAK1zsSNL",
        "d_JUdaOsKX4nf41Sp2L6r",
        "V0b7uBe4yNEoIC3wL21lD"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bAn",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2068158911,
      "version": 8953,
      "versionNonce": 1249122801,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792409321299,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TypeSafe AI's Workflow Evals benchmark, which evaluates how well Jev and conventional LLMs perform\non four business automation tasks requiring structured decisions.\n\n    1. Security Incident Management: Given a security alert and information about the affected device,\n        decide whether to close the incident, escalate it to an analyst, or contain the device immediately.\n    2. Agent Trace Observability: Examine an AI customer-support agent's execution trace, including its\n        tool calls, and decide whether human review is necessary and how urgently.\n    3. Invoice Processing: Compare a supplier invoice with the purchase order and delivered goods, then\n        decide whether to pay, hold, or reject the invoice.\n    4. Customer Service: Analyze a customer conversation and account information, then decide what the\n        assistant should do or say next.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJev achieves competitive accuracy at substantially lower cost than the other models evaluated.\n\nJev achieves almost the same accuracy as GPT Luna in workflow mode while costing approximately 7–8\ntimes less per case.\nMore capable reasoning models, such as GPT Sol and Claude Opus 5, achieve higher accuracy, around\n73–74%, but at significantly greater inference cost.\n\nTypeSafe reports the following end-to-end response times for structured decision-making workloads:\n\n    JEV / SYSTEM ONE: 70–500 ms\n    FRONTIER LLM WORKFLOWS: 3–5 s",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "TypeSafe AI's Workflow Evals benchmark, which evaluates how well Jev and conventional LLMs perform on four business automation tasks requiring structured decisions.\n\n    1. Security Incident Management: Given a security alert and information about the affected device,\n        decide whether to close the incident, escalate it to an analyst, or contain the device immediately.\n    2. Agent Trace Observability: Examine an AI customer-support agent's execution trace, including its\n        tool calls, and decide whether human review is necessary and how urgently.\n    3. Invoice Processing: Compare a supplier invoice with the purchase order and delivered goods, then\n        decide whether to pay, hold, or reject the invoice.\n    4. Customer Service: Analyze a customer conversation and account information, then decide what the\n        assistant should do or say next.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJev achieves competitive accuracy at substantially lower cost than the other models evaluated.\n\nJev achieves almost the same accuracy as GPT Luna in workflow mode while costing approximately 7–8 times less per case.\nMore capable reasoning models, such as GPT Sol and Claude Opus 5, achieve higher accuracy, around 73–74%, but at significantly greater inference cost.\n\nTypeSafe reports the following end-to-end response times for structured decision-making workloads:\n\n    JEV / SYSTEM ONE: 70–500 ms\n    FRONTIER LLM WORKFLOWS: 3–5 s",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1791878532392,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
